---
// about.astro — the full story, migrated from the WordPress About page.
// The profile photo and skill stack reveal on scroll (.reveal → GSAP).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About — Dylan K. Picart">
  <article class="post">
    <header>
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p style="color: var(--ink-soft); font-weight: 600;">
        Physicist and philosopher by training. Community-driven by design.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I'm a Data Engineer and researcher with a background in
        <strong>physics and philosophy</strong>, a combination that shapes how I
        approach every system I build: <strong>Analytical rigor, ethical
        intentionality, and a genuine commitment to the communities</strong> the
        data represents.
      </p>

      <!-- The portrait reveals as you scroll to it -->
      <div class="reveal portrait-wrap">
        <img class="portrait" src="/images/profile.jpg"
             alt="Dylan K. Picart" width="360" loading="lazy" />
      </div>

      <p>
        My work sits at the intersection of <strong>modern data engineering,
        scientific research, and social impact</strong>. I design
        <strong>cloud-native ETL/ELT</strong> pipelines, <strong>real-time
        streaming</strong> architectures, and AI-assisted analytics platforms
        that help mission-driven organizations turn fragmented, complex data
        into trustworthy, decision-ready insights. Recent work includes a
        real-time school climate and social vulnerability research platform
        investigating whether school climate indicators predict community
        vulnerability, independent citizen science research on SARS-CoV-2 RNA
        concentration patterns across 14 NYC wastewater sites, and
        peer-reviewed <strong>NLP</strong> research on large-scale image
        captioning datasets.
      </p>
      <p>
        Technically, I specialize in Python, SQL, Bash, PySpark, Snowflake,
        Databricks, Kafka, dbt, and Airflow, with production experience across
        GCP, AWS, and Azure. I've designed <strong>FERPA</strong> and
        <strong>HIPAA</strong>-aligned data governance frameworks, built RAG
        services using LangChain and vector databases, and developed NLP and
        classification models in PyTorch and scikit-learn.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also believe deeply in <strong>science communication and accessible
        education</strong>. As a Technical Instructor at The Knowledge House, 
        I currently teach Python, data science, web development, generative AI, 
        prompt engineering, and cybersecurity to teen and adult learners. I've 
        developed responsible AI and digital literacy curriculum covering 
        AI bias, cultural representation, privacy, and secure technology use. 
        Before that: ecology and environmental science in wilderness settings, 
        robotics and programming across all ages. Whether I'm designing a 
        medallion pipeline or facilitating a hands-on workshop, the goal is the 
        same: translate complexity into something that empowers people to 
        understand and act on the world around them.
      </p>
      <p>
        I care about <strong>data transparency, equity, and
        infrastructure</strong> that serves people rather than just processes.
        Whether I'm reconciling multi-source datasets to within 0.5% margin of
        error for grant reporting, migrating ten years of protected student
        records for social workers, or building dashboards that help leadership
        understand program impact across underserved communities, the through
        line is always the same: <strong>Data should strengthen trust and
        enable meaningful action.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of engineering, you'll find me <strong>running long distances,
        scuba diving, surfing, swimming, or practicing mindfulness</strong>.
        I'm always exploring unconventional learning pathways and curious,
        interdisciplinary conversations.
      </p>

      <h2>Skills</h2>
      <div class="reveal" style="text-align: center;">
        <img src="/images/skill-stack-logos.png" alt="Python, SQL, R, Bash, C, JavaScript, HTML, and CSS logos"
             width="440" loading="lazy" style="border: none; background: transparent;" />
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p><strong>Programming Languages:</strong> Python, SQL, Bash, R, C, YAML, Jinja2, JavaScript/TypeScript, HTML, CSS, Visual Basic, MATLAB</p>
        <p><strong>Data Analysis Tools:</strong> NumPy, Pandas, Matplotlib, Seaborn, Plotly, PowerBI, Tableau, ArcGIS, Excel</p>
        <p><strong>Machine Learning Frameworks:</strong> Scikit-learn, PyTorch, TensorFlow, Keras, LangChain, OpenAI API (LLMs &amp; embeddings), Vector Databases (Chroma), Prompt Engineering, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)</p>
        <p><strong>Data Engineering Tools:</strong> PySpark, Databricks, Delta Lake, dbt, Kafka, Snowflake, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, GraphQL, Hadoop, Apache Airflow, FastAPI microservices, Data Modeling (Bronze → Silver → Gold), Semantic Layer Design</p>
        <p><strong>Cloud, CRM, &amp; Version Control:</strong> GCP (GCS, Dataproc, IAM), AWS (S3, EMR), Azure, Docker, Terraform (IaC), Git, GitHub Actions (CI/CD), REST APIs, React/TypeScript (Vite), Full-stack Integration (API + Vector DB + LLM + UI), Salesforce, SharePoint, LaTeX, Apricot</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 0;"><strong>Soft Skills:</strong> Problem solving, detailed, team-oriented, business, scientific, and technical communication, ethical critical thinking, adaptable, leadership, conflict resolution</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Education</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Adelphi University</strong> — B.S. Physics, Minor in Philosophy
        (2014–2018). Specialization in Engineering, AI, and Data Analysis with
        advanced mathematics foundations. Year-round NCAA D-II Cross Country and
        Track &amp; Field athlete.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Fellowships &amp; Continuing Education:</strong> Program Earth
        Software Engineering Fellow (2024–Present) · TKH Data Science AEP
        Fellow, Data Engineering Track (2024) · TEC Innovate Google Fellow
        (2024) · CUNY GIS Research (2023)
      </p>

      <h2>Publications</h2>
      <p>
        Krotov, A., Tebo, A., <strong>Picart, D.</strong>, Algave, A. (2024).
        <em>Evaluating authenticity and quality of image captions via sentiment
        and semantic analyses.</em>
        <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.09560">arXiv:2409.09560</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Picart, D.</strong> (2018). <em>Method of Gas Detection
        Insensitive to Vibration.</em> Wright's Research Lab.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top: 3rem;">
        If you'd like to collaborate, brainstorm, or connect over data, AI, or
        community-focused innovation, feel free to
        <a href="/#contact">reach out</a> — I'd love to chat.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="btn" href="/resume/">See the full resume →</a>
        &nbsp;
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/dylanpicart">GitHub →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .portrait-wrap { text-align: center; margin: 2.5rem 0; }
  .portrait {
    width: min(360px, 80%);
    border-radius: 18px;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink) !important;
    box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 rgba(28, 27, 34, 0.15);
  }
</style>
